{"name":"Fields of Glory","hex":"#b18446","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fields","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of field"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of field"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fields"},{"term":"glory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Great beauty and splendor.","Honour, admiration, or distinction, accorded by common consent to a person or thing; high reputation; renown."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To exult with joy; to rejoice.","To boast; to be proud."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fields of Glory","blocks":[{"text":"Fields of Glory is a real-time strategy video game published by MicroProse for MS-DOS, Amiga and Amiga CD32 in 1993. In the game, players can re-enact the four major historical battles in Napoleon's Waterloo campaign, as well as play two hypothetical battles which would have possibly taken place had some of the pre-campaign maneuvering been done differently. The battles in the game are fought in real-time, and strive to create a sense of realism. It is based on a series of tabletop games of the same name."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ee/Fields_of_Glory_Coverart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fields_of_Glory"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"fields":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/En-us-fields.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d7/En-us-fields.ogg/En-us-fields.ogg.mp3"}],"glory":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/En-us-glory.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original